1
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:16,900
A man's collapsed.

2
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:20,600
The Whitmore Estate, the garden,
come in by the East Gate.

3
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:22,700
He's breathing, but only just.

4
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:24,100
Please hurry.

5
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:25,900
Stay with me.

6
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:28,900
Mornings, not evenings, remember?

7
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:35,600
Hannah, is he your father?

8
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:38,200
Yes.

9
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,400
Oh, he's just our old gardener.

10
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:43,400
Enjoy your dinner, ma'am.

11
00:01:12,494 --> 00:01:17,814
Dad. Dad, come here.
Halbrook. I got into Halbrook.

12
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:22,712
Read it to me. My hands are dirty.

13
00:01:23,322 --> 00:01:27,382
We are pleased to offer you
a place in the class of 2021.

14
00:01:27,812 --> 00:01:30,092
Pleased. They're pleased.

15
00:01:33,482 --> 00:01:37,672
$41,000. A year. That's just tuition, Dad.

16
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:38,742
Okay.

17
00:01:41,422 --> 00:01:44,582
Okay? That's more than you make.

18
00:01:45,831 --> 00:01:48,471
I said, okay, put the kettle on.

19
00:01:49,209 --> 00:01:52,242
I'll defer. I'll work a couple of years.

20
00:01:52,292 --> 00:01:53,572
You'll go.

21
00:01:56,842 --> 00:01:59,772
With what? You've got $11 in a coffee can.

22
00:01:59,822 --> 00:02:00,822
I've seen it.

23
00:02:01,202 --> 00:02:02,742
Then I'll find more.

24
00:02:07,852 --> 00:02:12,102
Dr. Castell, a nurse at
St. Mary's gave me your number.

25
00:02:12,152 --> 00:02:14,452
She said you pay for a kidney.

26
00:02:16,712 --> 00:02:20,312
Fifty-three. I don't drink,
I'm healthy as a horse.

27
00:02:26,761 --> 00:02:29,421
Forty. Yes, I can do Tuesday.

28
00:02:35,101 --> 00:02:37,461
You understand there's no taking it back.

29
00:02:38,419 --> 00:02:41,399
I've got two. She's got one shot.

30
00:02:44,267 --> 00:02:47,147
Most men who sit in that
chair are paying off a debt.

31
00:02:47,917 --> 00:02:52,037
I am. It's just not the
kind you're thinking of.

32
00:02:53,557 --> 00:02:57,277
Sign there. And Mr. Moore, we never met.

33
00:02:58,977 --> 00:03:00,317
Never met who?

34
00:03:22,187 --> 00:03:26,707
The Greenfield Foundation.
I've never even heard of them.

35
00:03:27,107 --> 00:03:30,327
Tuition, books, everything. Who does that?

36
00:03:31,136 --> 00:03:33,556
Rich people who feel guilty, probably.

37
00:03:40,404 --> 00:03:43,884
I'm going to find them.
I'm going to pay back every cent.

38
00:03:45,254 --> 00:03:49,054
Just go be good at it.
That's how you pay people back.

39
00:03:50,894 --> 00:03:54,084
Everybody there is going to have
parents who are judges and surgeons.

40
00:03:54,134 --> 00:03:56,434
And you'll have a dad who grows tomatoes.

41
00:03:57,914 --> 00:04:02,394
Listen to me. Dirt on your
hands is not dirt on your name.

42
00:04:03,194 --> 00:04:03,992
Hold your head up.

43
00:04:04,042 --> 00:04:07,962
Dirt on your hands, okay.

44
00:04:09,621 --> 00:04:11,481
Is not dirt on your name.

45
00:04:13,829 --> 00:04:15,869
Is not dirt on your name.

46
00:04:40,997 --> 00:04:44,557
Is that guy waving at you? Oh my god,
he wrapped them in newspaper.

47
00:04:48,046 --> 00:04:49,426
He's a friend of the family.

48
00:04:49,716 --> 00:04:51,776
Congratulations, Miss Moore.

49
00:04:53,186 --> 00:04:54,226
Ma'am.

50
00:05:09,355 --> 00:05:10,455
Did you eat?

51
00:05:11,625 --> 00:05:13,005
I'll grab something.

52
00:05:15,035 --> 00:05:16,495
That means no.

53
00:05:17,305 --> 00:05:22,005
Peanut butter. No banana,
the bananas are terrible this week.

54
00:05:22,755 --> 00:05:24,675
You don't have to keep doing this.

55
00:05:24,943 --> 00:05:29,023
Somebody does.
You'll faint in front of a judge.

56
00:05:43,902 --> 00:05:45,972
Sign where the yellow flags are.

57
00:05:46,022 --> 00:05:48,442
Whitmore trust, quarterly stuff.

58
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:52,752
That's a lot of quarterly stuff.

59
00:05:54,590 --> 00:05:58,630
Welcome to rich people. They move
money around the way we move furniture.

60
00:05:59,748 --> 00:06:04,808
Sunday. Lunch at my sister's.
You're not backing out on me.

61
00:06:06,607 --> 00:06:08,545
I'm terrified of your sister.

62
00:06:08,595 --> 00:06:11,175
Good. That means you've met her.

63
00:06:27,333 --> 00:06:28,813
Don't touch that.
Do you know what's in there?

64
00:06:30,333 --> 00:06:32,673
Sorry, sorry. I only clean around.

65
00:06:32,912 --> 00:06:35,097
Kyle. Her name is Mrs. Alvarez.

66
00:06:35,147 --> 00:06:37,765
She's been here longer than you have.

67
00:06:37,815 --> 00:06:41,792
She's emptied your trash
every night for two years.

68
00:06:42,452 --> 00:06:43,972
Say thank you.

69
00:06:44,512 --> 00:06:45,512
Thank you.

70
00:06:49,482 --> 00:06:51,682
You didn't have to do that, Miss Moore.

71
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:57,880
My dad always says nobody notices the people
who keep things clean until they stop.

72
00:06:58,470 --> 00:07:02,150
Your father sounds like a smart man.

73
00:07:02,428 --> 00:07:03,428
He is.

74
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:24,593
Is that a peanut butter sandwich?

75
00:07:25,093 --> 00:07:25,895
You're a lawyer.

76
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:27,345
Lawyers eat.

77
00:07:28,382 --> 00:07:31,862
Lawyers expense lunch. Who packed it?

78
00:07:31,942 --> 00:07:33,162
My dad.

79
00:07:33,868 --> 00:07:35,668
He cut the crusts off.

80
00:07:35,933 --> 00:07:37,573
He thinks I'm nine.

81
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:40,320
I'm Julian. I design buildings.

82
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:43,270
Not this one.

83
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:46,660
Hannah! I argue in this one.

84
00:07:46,810 --> 00:07:49,410
Then let me buy you a lunch nobody packed.

85
00:07:50,570 --> 00:07:51,588
Dinner, technically.

86
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:53,538
You don't even know my last name.

87
00:07:53,903 --> 00:07:55,583
That's what dinner's for.

88
00:08:08,378 --> 00:08:10,825
Julian says you grew up in the city.

89
00:08:10,875 --> 00:08:11,938
Which part?

90
00:08:15,087 --> 00:08:17,827
East side. Near the river.

91
00:08:18,295 --> 00:08:20,875
Oh. Near the river.

92
00:08:23,295 --> 00:08:24,295
And your parents?

93
00:08:28,263 --> 00:08:30,403
My mom died when I was nine.

94
00:08:31,212 --> 00:08:34,232
I'm sorry. And your father?

95
00:08:36,212 --> 00:08:40,252
He's retired. He travels a lot.

96
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:44,280
What's his handicap?

97
00:08:47,215 --> 00:08:48,375
I'm sorry?

98
00:08:49,253 --> 00:08:52,813
She means golf, Mom.
Not everybody plays golf.

99
00:08:52,962 --> 00:08:57,422
She never lets me meet him.
I'm starting to think he doesn't exist.

100
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:00,880
Or he's met your mother.

101
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:06,360
Walter. There's a fingerprint on this.

102
00:09:08,607 --> 00:09:09,607
Apologies, madam.

103
00:09:10,857 --> 00:09:12,989
She asked me what my
father's handicap was.

104
00:09:13,039 --> 00:09:14,557
I nearly said bad knees.

105
00:09:14,607 --> 00:09:18,313
It went great. She only checked
one glass for fingerprints.

106
00:09:18,363 --> 00:09:19,427
That's love.

107
00:09:19,837 --> 00:09:22,179
I had a whole plan. A violinist, a boat.

108
00:09:22,229 --> 00:09:26,477
I'm doing it in my parents' driveway
because I can't wait anymore.

109
00:09:27,597 --> 00:09:30,437
Julian, get up, you're kneeling on gravel.

110
00:09:31,755 --> 00:09:33,075
Is that a yes?

111
00:09:33,295 --> 00:09:36,575
Yes. Yes. Get up.

112
00:09:41,075 --> 00:09:42,766
Mom wants an engagement dinner.

113
00:09:42,816 --> 00:09:45,475
I said you'd host. Your place, your rules.

114
00:09:47,165 --> 00:09:48,345
My place?

115
00:09:49,625 --> 00:09:52,525
Well, look at that. He did good.

116
00:09:53,353 --> 00:09:54,773
He did okay.

117
00:09:55,463 --> 00:09:58,516
Your mother got a ring
out of a gumball machine.

118
00:09:58,566 --> 00:10:00,223
Wore it eleven years.

119
00:10:01,583 --> 00:10:03,483
The dinner's Saturday. Here.

120
00:10:04,513 --> 00:10:06,353
I'll get the grey suit cleaned.

121
00:10:07,803 --> 00:10:09,523
About that.

122
00:10:10,513 --> 00:10:12,193
Would you mind staying in the cottage?

123
00:10:12,243 --> 00:10:14,013
Just for the dinner. It's not about you.

124
00:10:14,063 --> 00:10:15,773
They're just, Celeste is a lot.

125
00:10:20,245 --> 00:10:22,785
I'll make sure the roses
look nice from the window.

126
00:10:24,343 --> 00:10:25,343
Dad.

127
00:10:26,063 --> 00:10:28,223
It's fine. I'll watch the game.

128
00:10:32,591 --> 00:10:35,002
Two servers. Two! On a Saturday.

129
00:10:35,052 --> 00:10:40,811
I have six courses and a lady in
green who already sent back the bread.

130
00:10:42,049 --> 00:10:43,509
Where are the aprons?

131
00:10:45,239 --> 00:10:46,359
Who are you?

132
00:10:46,959 --> 00:10:47,925
I live out back.

133
00:10:47,975 --> 00:10:52,339
I've carried trays at more weddings
than you've had hot dinners.

134
00:10:53,848 --> 00:10:55,208
You're an angel.

135
00:10:57,268 --> 00:10:58,768
Don't tell my daughter.

136
00:10:59,818 --> 00:11:01,998
Still no father tonight, Hannah?

137
00:11:02,603 --> 00:11:05,103
He's away. Portugal.

138
00:11:05,763 --> 00:11:08,423
Portugal. In November.

139
00:11:09,303 --> 00:11:10,303
Mom.

140
00:11:23,363 --> 00:11:25,423
And who's this? He's very good.

141
00:11:27,723 --> 00:11:30,483
Oh, he's just our old gardener.

142
00:11:32,193 --> 00:11:34,853
Well, he pours better than he dresses.

143
00:11:42,303 --> 00:11:43,803
Enjoy your dinner, ma'am.

144
00:12:06,381 --> 00:12:07,421
You okay?

145
00:12:08,321 --> 00:12:11,661
Never better. They liked the wine.

146
00:12:13,019 --> 00:12:15,599
I'm hiding. Don't tell anyone.

147
00:12:16,978 --> 00:12:19,058
Hiding's free back here.

148
00:12:21,008 --> 00:12:21,607
Those roses.

149
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:27,528
My mother's been through three gardeners in five years,
and none of them could grow anything like that.

150
00:12:28,296 --> 00:12:32,556
Don't fuss them.
Most people fuss roses to death.

151
00:12:33,226 --> 00:12:35,626
That's it? That's the secret?

152
00:12:37,103 --> 00:12:39,333
That, and my wife planted that one.

153
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:41,229
It'd be rude to die on her.

154
00:12:41,279 --> 00:12:42,279
Julian.

155
00:12:46,789 --> 00:12:49,449
Elijah. Nice to meet you, sir.

156
00:12:50,479 --> 00:12:54,279
Please don't call me sir.
My mother'll hear and think it's working.

157
00:13:04,799 --> 00:13:06,219
You're still up.

158
00:13:06,939 --> 00:13:11,219
Slugs come out at night.
Somebody has to tell them no.

159
00:13:12,099 --> 00:13:13,539
Dad, about tonight.

160
00:13:14,899 --> 00:13:18,259
The lamb was good. Delia can cook.

161
00:13:20,203 --> 00:13:21,203
Dad.

162
00:13:23,013 --> 00:13:27,381
I heard you. I've been
called worse by better.

163
00:13:27,431 --> 00:13:33,510
You don't know these people.
If she knew, she'd look at me different.

164
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:34,571
Forever.

165
00:13:35,459 --> 00:13:43,559
Maybe. Go to bed. You've got a
wedding to plan, and I've got slugs.

166
00:13:49,588 --> 00:13:52,068
Your girl's getting married, Miriam.

167
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:55,500
Who does these?

168
00:13:56,810 --> 00:13:58,190
Our gardener.

169
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,520
Your wine man.

170
00:14:02,130 --> 00:14:04,670
You. What do you charge?

171
00:14:06,610 --> 00:14:08,350
Depends on the garden, ma'am.

172
00:14:10,990 --> 00:14:14,861
Mine's a disgrace, and there's
a wedding in it in nine weeks.

173
00:14:14,911 --> 00:14:16,690
Twenty an hour. Monday.

174
00:14:16,998 --> 00:14:18,098
Twenty-two.

175
00:14:24,188 --> 00:14:26,217
I'm worth the two dollars, ma'am.

176
00:14:26,267 --> 00:14:27,448
Ask the roses.

177
00:14:27,768 --> 00:14:31,268
Twenty-two. And you'll use the side gate.

178
00:14:32,117 --> 00:14:34,614
One more thing. The wedding arch.

179
00:14:34,664 --> 00:14:37,357
I'd want to grow it from these.

180
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:39,780
Fine. Make it pretty.

181
00:14:43,138 --> 00:14:44,378
Dad, what are you doing?

182
00:14:44,968 --> 00:14:46,408
Gettin' a raise.

183
00:14:49,608 --> 00:14:50,848
I'm serious.

184
00:14:52,038 --> 00:14:56,017
So am I. You're getting
married under something I grew.

185
00:14:56,067 --> 00:14:58,218
Don't you take that from me.

186
00:14:58,268 --> 00:15:00,381
Side gate. Always the side gate.

187
00:15:00,431 --> 00:15:02,340
Boots off before the terrace.

188
00:15:02,390 --> 00:15:07,488
You don't speak to the family unless
they speak to you, and they won't.

189
00:15:09,248 --> 00:15:10,288
Yes, sir.

190
00:15:11,648 --> 00:15:14,141
And the roses on the east wall are dead.

191
00:15:14,191 --> 00:15:16,747
She'll tell you it was the last gardener.

192
00:15:16,797 --> 00:15:19,448
It was her. She waters them at night.

193
00:15:21,257 --> 00:15:23,137
Evenings. That'll do it.

194
00:15:23,577 --> 00:15:27,397
Walter. Not sir. I only dress like one.

195
00:15:57,595 --> 00:15:58,595
Boots.

196
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:01,060
Ma'am?

197
00:16:02,017 --> 00:16:04,277
You're on my terrace in boots.

198
00:16:06,557 --> 00:16:08,433
Just cutting through to the shed, ma'am.

199
00:16:08,483 --> 00:16:09,483
I'll go round.

200
00:16:12,518 --> 00:16:14,198
Since you're here.

201
00:16:21,345 --> 00:16:23,645
Well, I can't use it now, can I?

202
00:16:30,465 --> 00:16:31,465
Afternoon, Miss Moore.

203
00:16:32,513 --> 00:16:33,733
Afternoon.

204
00:16:39,010 --> 00:16:41,070
You don't have to let her do that.

205
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:44,400
Neither do you.

206
00:16:46,910 --> 00:16:48,210
That's not fair.

207
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:50,740
No. It isn't.

208
00:16:56,826 --> 00:17:00,723
No, listen to me. Listen.
It's three point two, not three.

209
00:17:00,773 --> 00:17:04,602
Nobody's going to look past
her name, it's on every page.

210
00:17:04,652 --> 00:17:07,266
I made sure she signed in a hurry.

211
00:17:11,403 --> 00:17:13,983
Because she's a nobody, Danny. No family.

212
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,972
A dad who's always in Portugal.

213
00:17:16,022 --> 00:17:18,183
Who's going to fight for her?

214
00:17:23,514 --> 00:17:25,958
And on Friday I'm making her partner.

215
00:17:26,008 --> 00:17:30,014
A partner's signature hangs
better than an associate's.

216
00:17:31,284 --> 00:17:36,634
The wedding? Celeste will cancel it
herself the minute anybody says fraud.

217
00:17:36,684 --> 00:17:38,224
I know my sister.

218
00:17:44,133 --> 00:17:45,153
Who's there?

219
00:17:45,723 --> 00:17:49,563
Just me, sir. Deadheading.

220
00:17:50,841 --> 00:17:52,601
How long have you been back there?

221
00:17:54,001 --> 00:17:56,236
Long enough to get the whites done.

222
00:17:56,286 --> 00:17:57,761
The reds are next.

223
00:17:59,071 --> 00:18:03,171
Good roses. Shame if you
got careless with those.

224
00:18:16,511 --> 00:18:17,751
Sit down a minute.

225
00:18:19,161 --> 00:18:21,941
Dad, it's eleven.
I've got a deposition at eight.

226
00:18:23,159 --> 00:18:25,499
Marcus was on the phone
in the garden today.

227
00:18:25,859 --> 00:18:26,859
Okay.

228
00:18:28,969 --> 00:18:30,956
He said three point two million.

229
00:18:31,006 --> 00:18:33,119
He said your name's on every page.

230
00:18:33,169 --> 00:18:36,969
He said you're a nobody and
nobody would fight for you.

231
00:18:37,793 --> 00:18:39,593
He would never say that.

232
00:18:41,403 --> 00:18:43,603
He said it to a man called Danny.

233
00:18:43,833 --> 00:18:47,066
Dad. Marcus has been
good to me for six years.

234
00:18:47,116 --> 00:18:51,913
My first winter, he bought me a
coat because I didn't have one.

235
00:18:54,001 --> 00:18:55,701
Did you read what you signed?

236
00:18:58,291 --> 00:19:00,611
You heard half a phone
call through a hedge.

237
00:19:02,071 --> 00:19:03,731
I heard what I heard.

238
00:19:06,361 --> 00:19:07,688
And what do I do with that?

239
00:19:07,738 --> 00:19:11,761
Walk into Richard Whitmore's office
and say the gardener heard something?

240
00:19:13,171 --> 00:19:15,031
I didn't mean—

241
00:19:17,041 --> 00:19:20,141
Yes, you did. It's all right. It's late.

242
00:19:27,461 --> 00:19:31,001
Because she's a nobody, Danny. No family.

243
00:19:40,231 --> 00:19:41,891
Get down from there.

244
00:19:43,899 --> 00:19:45,199
Two more ties.

245
00:19:46,729 --> 00:19:50,560
Get down before I have to explain
a dead gardener to Mrs. Whitmore.

246
00:19:50,610 --> 00:19:52,589
She'll want it off the books.

247
00:20:01,099 --> 00:20:03,639
Your ankles are the size of my head.

248
00:20:05,988 --> 00:20:07,168
It's the heat.

249
00:20:08,228 --> 00:20:11,388
It's not the heat. See a doctor.

250
00:20:12,466 --> 00:20:15,530
A hundred and eighty
dollars to be told to rest.

251
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:18,346
I can rest for free when this is done.

252
00:20:29,036 --> 00:20:31,596
You look at her the way I
look at my granddaughter.

253
00:20:32,376 --> 00:20:34,016
None of my business.

254
00:20:35,246 --> 00:20:37,926
No. It isn't.

255
00:20:40,076 --> 00:20:41,676
Drink your water.

256
00:20:50,306 --> 00:20:52,246
Night, Dad.

257
00:20:53,526 --> 00:20:55,686
Night, baby girl. Eat something.

258
00:21:16,184 --> 00:21:17,704
Can I help you, sir?

259
00:21:21,002 --> 00:21:22,742
Looking for the gardener.

260
00:21:25,501 --> 00:21:27,101
In his coat, sir?

261
00:21:27,621 --> 00:21:29,301
Tell him I'd like a word.

262
00:21:42,331 --> 00:21:49,091
Sit. Good news first. The partnership vote
is Friday and I'm putting your name in.

263
00:21:49,811 --> 00:21:53,011
Marcus, are you serious?

264
00:21:53,349 --> 00:21:55,769
Youngest partner in the firm's history.

265
00:22:03,707 --> 00:22:04,847
How's Portugal?

266
00:22:09,366 --> 00:22:13,986
I'm not judging. Everybody's
embarrassed of something.

267
00:22:14,646 --> 00:22:17,066
My mother sold lipstick
out of a station wagon.

268
00:22:17,134 --> 00:22:18,434
What do you want?

269
00:22:20,752 --> 00:22:23,202
Your father's been
crouching in hedges on my

270
00:22:23,252 --> 00:22:25,972
sister's property,
listening to private calls.

271
00:22:26,512 --> 00:22:28,792
If Celeste finds out,
she calls the police.

272
00:22:29,657 --> 00:22:32,827
Then she asks why her
son's fiancée lied to her

273
00:22:32,877 --> 00:22:36,737
face at her own table,
and that's the wedding.

274
00:22:38,166 --> 00:22:40,026
He's not. He wouldn't.

275
00:22:41,354 --> 00:22:46,134
I want him off the estate.
And I don't want to see him at the wedding.

276
00:22:46,574 --> 00:22:49,754
Not serving, not standing
at the back. Nowhere.

277
00:22:51,314 --> 00:22:54,814
He's building the arch. It's his arch.

278
00:22:56,534 --> 00:22:58,814
Then it'll be a very nice arch.

279
00:23:01,292 --> 00:23:03,962
Friday, Hannah,
think about how far you've come,

280
00:23:04,012 --> 00:23:06,912
and whatever he thinks he heard,
make sure he forgets it.

281
00:23:09,752 --> 00:23:11,472
Dad, I need you to...

282
00:23:22,261 --> 00:23:23,641
You eat?

283
00:23:25,691 --> 00:23:26,691
Yeah.

284
00:23:33,251 --> 00:23:35,691
Dad, I need you to stop
going to the estate.

285
00:23:37,711 --> 00:23:39,611
The arch is two weeks from done.

286
00:23:39,791 --> 00:23:41,731
Somebody else can finish it.

287
00:23:45,409 --> 00:23:47,609
Nobody else knows those roses.

288
00:23:53,959 --> 00:23:55,599
Who told you to say this?

289
00:23:58,019 --> 00:23:59,739
Nobody told me anything.

290
00:24:02,007 --> 00:24:03,007
Marcus?

291
00:24:03,627 --> 00:24:07,357
It doesn't matter who.
If Celeste finds out you're

292
00:24:07,407 --> 00:24:10,647
my father after I lied
to her face, it's over.

293
00:24:12,307 --> 00:24:15,467
And she could have you arrested
for what you did in that garden.

294
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:17,227
I'm trying to protect you.

295
00:24:20,327 --> 00:24:21,327
Okay.

296
00:24:23,247 --> 00:24:24,467
And the wedding?

297
00:24:28,767 --> 00:24:30,467
I don't think you should come.

298
00:24:39,006 --> 00:24:40,226
To the wedding?

299
00:24:40,586 --> 00:24:44,036
You'd be working it anyway.
She thinks you're staff.

300
00:24:44,086 --> 00:24:46,466
You'd be carrying trays
at your own daughter's.

301
00:24:49,294 --> 00:24:51,194
I'd have carried them.

302
00:24:53,044 --> 00:24:58,064
I know you would, I know.
That's why I can't let you.

303
00:25:03,777 --> 00:25:04,917
All right.

304
00:25:06,527 --> 00:25:07,527
Dad.

305
00:25:08,704 --> 00:25:12,604
I said, all right, go in. It's cold.

306
00:25:24,214 --> 00:25:25,994
Monday's my last day.

307
00:25:27,804 --> 00:25:29,784
The arch isn't finished.

308
00:25:32,432 --> 00:25:33,472
I know.

309
00:25:35,342 --> 00:25:36,982
Did she fire you?

310
00:25:38,572 --> 00:25:41,832
Nobody fired me. Family things.

311
00:25:42,632 --> 00:25:44,072
Family things.

312
00:25:49,652 --> 00:25:51,661
You keep touching that pocket.

313
00:25:51,711 --> 00:25:52,851
Something I heard.

314
00:25:53,971 --> 00:25:57,051
If I play it, everybody
finds out she lied about me.

315
00:25:58,071 --> 00:26:01,791
Then she loses the wedding anyway,
just from the other side.

316
00:26:02,537 --> 00:26:04,257
So you do nothing.

317
00:26:05,697 --> 00:26:07,697
I finish the arch.

318
00:26:11,131 --> 00:26:13,831
The East Gate isn't locked before six.

319
00:26:13,891 --> 00:26:16,591
I'm up at five. Nobody else is.

320
00:26:18,519 --> 00:26:20,339
Why would I need to know that?

321
00:26:21,269 --> 00:26:22,949
No reason at all.

322
00:26:51,789 --> 00:26:55,279
To the youngest partner in
the history of this firm.

323
00:27:16,537 --> 00:27:19,317
There you go, Miriam. All done.

324
00:27:37,517 --> 00:27:42,847
A man's collapsed. The Whitmore Estate,
the garden, come in by the East Gate.

325
00:27:42,897 --> 00:27:45,637
He's breathing,
but only just. Please hurry.

326
00:27:49,475 --> 00:27:53,715
Stay with me. Mornings,
not evenings, remember?

327
00:27:53,975 --> 00:27:55,595
Who's going to water the thing?

328
00:27:57,055 --> 00:28:02,245
Mr. Julian, it's Walter, it's the
gardener, he's going to St. Mary's.

329
00:28:02,295 --> 00:28:05,695
Sir, I think you'd better tell Miss Moore,
I think he's her father.

330
00:28:13,053 --> 00:28:16,893
Hannah. Walter found Elijah in the garden.

331
00:28:17,073 --> 00:28:18,513
He's on his way to St. Mary's.

332
00:28:22,592 --> 00:28:25,632
Hannah, is he your father?

333
00:28:27,760 --> 00:28:28,780
Yes.

334
00:28:29,368 --> 00:28:33,708
Pressure's 210 over 120.
Get a line in, call nephrology.

335
00:28:39,407 --> 00:28:40,727
Are you family?

336
00:28:42,127 --> 00:28:45,017
I'm his daughter, Elijah Moore.

337
00:28:45,067 --> 00:28:46,067
He's my father.

338
00:28:49,447 --> 00:28:51,747
Your father's kidney is failing.

339
00:28:52,067 --> 00:28:53,567
It's very advanced.

340
00:28:54,417 --> 00:28:56,667
Kidney? Kidneys?

341
00:28:56,907 --> 00:28:59,647
No. He only has one.

342
00:28:59,877 --> 00:29:03,937
That's not right. He's never had surgery.

343
00:29:04,137 --> 00:29:06,057
He's never been sick a day in his life.

344
00:29:06,185 --> 00:29:08,445
There's a scar on his left side.

345
00:29:08,725 --> 00:29:10,845
It's old. Seven or eight years.

346
00:29:12,125 --> 00:29:15,805
Somebody took a kidney out of your father
and they knew what they were doing.

347
00:29:20,483 --> 00:29:22,823
Eight years ago,
I was starting law school.

348
00:29:23,072 --> 00:29:26,372
The man who brought him in
said he's been working nights.

349
00:29:26,692 --> 00:29:29,632
In the cold. With his kidney like this,

350
00:29:29,792 --> 00:29:31,712
that's the last thing he
should have been doing.

351
00:29:32,682 --> 00:29:34,242
Working on what?

352
00:29:34,812 --> 00:29:36,612
He said an arch.

353
00:29:42,042 --> 00:29:45,002
Without a transplant, we're talking weeks.

354
00:29:45,702 --> 00:29:47,522
Dialysis will buy us some time.

355
00:29:48,162 --> 00:29:49,682
Is there any other family?

356
00:29:50,540 --> 00:29:52,160
It's just me.

357
00:29:57,440 --> 00:30:00,720
His things. The coat's wet, I'm sorry.

358
00:30:05,758 --> 00:30:09,218
Hannah, I'm so sorry to do this today.

359
00:30:10,298 --> 00:30:13,858
The auditors found 3.2 million
missing from the Whitmore Trust.

360
00:30:14,358 --> 00:30:15,838
Every transfer has your signature.

361
00:30:16,757 --> 00:30:19,037
Marcus, I signed what
you put in front of me.

362
00:30:19,535 --> 00:30:24,055
Then you should have read it.
You're suspended, effective now.

363
00:30:24,295 --> 00:30:25,295
Don't come in.

364
00:30:27,083 --> 00:30:29,243
I did what you asked. I sent him away.

365
00:30:29,472 --> 00:30:32,872
And I appreciate it.
Read before you sign, Hannah.

366
00:30:37,442 --> 00:30:39,102
He tried to tell me.

367
00:31:21,631 --> 00:31:28,951
Greenfield, you made it up.
You spelled pleased wrong.

368
00:31:36,539 --> 00:31:38,439
I called you the gardener.

369
00:31:42,749 --> 00:31:48,069
Fraud, Julian. Three million dollars,
it'll be in every paper by tomorrow.

370
00:31:49,287 --> 00:31:50,667
She didn't do it.

371
00:31:51,677 --> 00:31:53,797
Marcus says the signatures.

372
00:31:55,027 --> 00:31:56,467
Marcus says.

373
00:31:57,797 --> 00:32:01,757
The wedding is off.
I'm calling the planner tonight.

374
00:32:02,297 --> 00:32:05,597
Call whoever you like.
I'm still marrying her.

375
00:32:05,672 --> 00:32:09,892
With what? Your father will cut you off.

376
00:32:10,891 --> 00:32:12,971
Then I'll be poor and married.

377
00:32:24,689 --> 00:32:26,329
He's not the gardener.

378
00:32:26,947 --> 00:32:30,657
I know. I should have
seen it at the dinner.

379
00:32:30,707 --> 00:32:34,087
He filled your glass last.
Nobody does that for a stranger.

380
00:32:38,506 --> 00:32:44,046
He sold his kidney, Julian,
for law school, $40,000.

381
00:32:44,826 --> 00:32:46,726
He told me it was a scholarship.

382
00:32:47,444 --> 00:32:51,464
He made up a whole foundation
and he spelled pleased wrong.

383
00:32:52,084 --> 00:32:55,204
And Marcus showed me a picture
and offered me partner,

384
00:32:55,724 --> 00:32:59,284
and I went home and told my
father not to come to my wedding.

385
00:33:00,044 --> 00:33:01,304
And he said, all right.

386
00:33:02,202 --> 00:33:05,062
And then he went and finished
the arch in the dark,

387
00:33:05,402 --> 00:33:08,162
so it'd be ready for a wedding
he wasn't allowed to see.

388
00:33:09,112 --> 00:33:11,352
I traded my father for a title.

389
00:33:12,721 --> 00:33:14,541
Why?

390
00:33:17,281 --> 00:33:19,521
Because the first time it was easier.

391
00:33:20,241 --> 00:33:21,441
And then it was a habit.

392
00:33:23,309 --> 00:33:25,069
Do you still want to marry me?

393
00:33:26,757 --> 00:33:27,757
Yes.

394
00:33:28,667 --> 00:33:30,507
Then I want to meet your father.

395
00:33:31,267 --> 00:33:34,467
Properly. Not the wine man. Your dad.

396
00:33:34,916 --> 00:33:36,816
He's dying, Julian.

397
00:33:38,556 --> 00:33:40,196
Then we'd better hurry.

398
00:33:44,451 --> 00:33:46,991
If you're a match,
I'll be honest with you.

399
00:33:47,731 --> 00:33:49,251
It's not a small surgery.

400
00:33:50,769 --> 00:33:52,209
Neither was his.

401
00:34:01,293 --> 00:34:05,793
Mr. Moore, we have a match,
a very good one.

402
00:34:06,103 --> 00:34:07,443
Somebody died.

403
00:34:07,676 --> 00:34:10,416
No, a living donor.

404
00:34:13,896 --> 00:34:14,896
No.

405
00:34:16,706 --> 00:34:17,261
Dad.

406
00:34:17,311 --> 00:34:20,931
No, Doctor. She's getting married.

407
00:34:21,391 --> 00:34:22,391
Tell her no.

408
00:34:23,451 --> 00:34:25,131
I'll give you two a minute.

409
00:34:29,901 --> 00:34:31,481
I found the box.

410
00:34:33,001 --> 00:34:37,281
The Greenfield Foundation.
You spelt pleased wrong.

411
00:34:38,061 --> 00:34:39,661
Eight years, Dad.

412
00:34:41,281 --> 00:34:42,971
Every time I bought a
nice coat, every time

413
00:34:43,021 --> 00:34:45,141
I walked into court,
I thought, look at me.

414
00:34:45,270 --> 00:34:49,250
I did this. I did all of this by myself.

415
00:34:49,790 --> 00:34:51,410
And you let me think that.

416
00:34:52,618 --> 00:34:56,078
You did do it. I just paid the fee.

417
00:34:58,008 --> 00:35:02,608
You paid with your body. And I told
them you were a friend of the family.

418
00:35:02,768 --> 00:35:04,468
Then I told them you were the gardener.

419
00:35:04,966 --> 00:35:07,266
Then I told you not to come to my wedding.

420
00:35:07,726 --> 00:35:10,126
Three times. I count all three.

421
00:35:10,385 --> 00:35:11,685
I don't.

422
00:35:14,565 --> 00:35:15,665
I do.

423
00:35:20,285 --> 00:35:22,455
You always told me to hold my head up.

424
00:35:22,505 --> 00:35:27,385
I can't. Not if you die in here because
I was too ashamed to say your name.

425
00:35:27,953 --> 00:35:32,183
So I'm gonna say it to anybody
who'll listen and you're gonna

426
00:35:32,233 --> 00:35:35,121
take my kidney and you're
gonna walk me down that aisle.

427
00:35:35,171 --> 00:35:41,111
And you're not going to argue with me
because I'm a lawyer and I will win.

428
00:35:44,490 --> 00:35:46,110
You're your mother.

429
00:35:47,380 --> 00:35:48,740
Is that a yes?

430
00:35:51,400 --> 00:35:53,860
Your mother never let me say no either.

431
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:05,840
You scared?

432
00:36:08,570 --> 00:36:09,950
Terrified.

433
00:36:10,610 --> 00:36:14,910
Me too. First time I did this,
I was by myself.

434
00:36:15,610 --> 00:36:16,710
This is better.

435
00:36:31,710 --> 00:36:35,250
Dad, what are you doing here?

436
00:36:36,148 --> 00:36:40,068
Walter told me about the gardener.

437
00:36:42,238 --> 00:36:44,178
Your mother doesn't know I'm here.

438
00:36:45,586 --> 00:36:46,966
Are you gonna tell her?

439
00:36:47,786 --> 00:36:51,966
Eventually, I'd like to see her face.

440
00:37:02,136 --> 00:37:05,836
It's working.
It started working on the table.

441
00:37:10,786 --> 00:37:14,066
His coat. Walter brought it.

442
00:37:19,395 --> 00:37:22,040
Because she's a nobody, Danny. No family.

443
00:37:22,090 --> 00:37:24,078
A dad who's always in Portugal.

444
00:37:24,128 --> 00:37:26,335
Who's going to fight for her?

445
00:37:29,518 --> 00:37:34,598
He recorded it. He recorded it and I
told him he heard half a phone call.

446
00:37:36,216 --> 00:37:37,496
That's my uncle.

447
00:37:38,956 --> 00:37:40,296
That's evidence.

448
00:37:45,676 --> 00:37:50,236
From the arch. I watered
it mornings, not evenings.

449
00:37:50,456 --> 00:37:51,776
You remembered.

450
00:37:54,741 --> 00:37:59,341
Walter, did anybody
ever ask you about this?

451
00:38:03,801 --> 00:38:05,911
Mr. Hale went through
his coat in the potting

452
00:38:05,961 --> 00:38:08,481
shed, the week before he stopped coming.

453
00:38:08,570 --> 00:38:12,890
Every pocket. I asked if I could help him.

454
00:38:13,150 --> 00:38:14,270
He didn't like that.

455
00:38:15,718 --> 00:38:17,358
He was looking for this.

456
00:38:18,878 --> 00:38:22,438
Then I'll say so,
to whoever needs to hear it.

457
00:38:27,267 --> 00:38:30,847
I'll keep this short because it's painful.

458
00:38:32,187 --> 00:38:35,447
Every transfer, every single
one was signed by Hannah Moore.

459
00:38:36,265 --> 00:38:38,285
I brought her into this family.

460
00:38:38,805 --> 00:38:40,505
I take responsibility for that.

461
00:38:41,525 --> 00:38:43,175
You couldn't have known, Marcus.

462
00:38:43,225 --> 00:38:44,225
I should have.

463
00:38:46,585 --> 00:38:49,345
Richard, I'd recommend we hand this
to the district attorney today.

464
00:38:49,484 --> 00:38:52,224
No rush. We have time.

465
00:38:58,482 --> 00:39:01,422
Hannah, you shouldn't be here.

466
00:39:01,602 --> 00:39:03,742
I'm still a member of the bar.
Sit down, Marcus.

467
00:39:05,952 --> 00:39:07,092
This one's short, too.

468
00:39:18,650 --> 00:39:20,870
That's a cheap phone and a hedge.

469
00:39:21,210 --> 00:39:22,290
That could be anybody.

470
00:39:23,460 --> 00:39:27,280
It's you, talking to Danny
Coyle at First Harbor Bank.

471
00:39:28,490 --> 00:39:31,250
We traced the money this
morning, Mr. Chairman.

472
00:39:31,610 --> 00:39:34,290
The account it went to
is in Mr. Hale's name.

473
00:39:35,780 --> 00:39:36,800
Marcus.

474
00:39:38,270 --> 00:39:39,670
Celeste.

475
00:39:40,370 --> 00:39:41,370
Walter?

476
00:39:43,839 --> 00:39:48,199
Mr. Hale searched the gardener's coat
in the potting shed, sir, every pocket.

477
00:39:48,399 --> 00:39:49,799
He was looking for that phone.

478
00:39:50,907 --> 00:39:53,047
You're taking the word of a butler?

479
00:39:53,227 --> 00:39:56,907
For 31 years. Sit down, Marcus.

480
00:39:57,285 --> 00:40:01,905
The gardener. Why would the gardener
be in the hedge with a phone?

481
00:40:02,225 --> 00:40:05,725
Because he's my father, Elijah Moore.

482
00:40:08,684 --> 00:40:12,544
Marcus found out. He made me partner.

483
00:40:13,204 --> 00:40:15,704
And the price was that my father
didn't come to my wedding.

484
00:40:17,144 --> 00:40:22,624
I said yes. He finished your son's
arch at four in the morning by himself.

485
00:40:22,794 --> 00:40:24,914
And then he collapsed under it.

486
00:40:26,714 --> 00:40:28,914
That's the man you made
pick up your napkin.

487
00:40:33,422 --> 00:40:35,002
I made you partner.

488
00:40:35,982 --> 00:40:37,262
I resign.

489
00:40:41,382 --> 00:40:42,682
Marcus Hale.

490
00:40:44,612 --> 00:40:46,552
I gave you everything.

491
00:40:47,860 --> 00:40:51,360
You gave me a coat. He gave me a kidney.

492
00:40:56,130 --> 00:41:00,630
All in favor of clearing Miss Moore
and removing Mr. Hale as trustee.

493
00:41:06,810 --> 00:41:12,730
One more. I move that Celeste Whitmore
be removed from the trust board.

494
00:41:14,749 --> 00:41:15,749
Richard.

495
00:41:16,439 --> 00:41:18,979
You defended him for an hour, Celeste.

496
00:41:19,659 --> 00:41:21,719
You never once asked the gardener's name.

497
00:41:33,497 --> 00:41:35,897
Why didn't he just tell me who he was?

498
00:41:37,517 --> 00:41:40,817
Because I asked him not to.
That part's on me.

499
00:41:43,457 --> 00:41:46,357
I would never have spoken to
him like that if I'd known.

500
00:41:48,017 --> 00:41:50,597
I know. That's the problem.

501
00:42:05,721 --> 00:42:07,971
Your mother would have cried
through the whole thing.

502
00:42:08,021 --> 00:42:10,861
You're crying.

503
00:42:11,021 --> 00:42:13,381
Pollen.

504
00:42:31,559 --> 00:42:32,779
Thank you, sir.

505
00:42:33,699 --> 00:42:37,059
Elijah, or Dad if you're brave.

506
00:42:37,959 --> 00:42:39,659
You may kiss the bride.

507
00:42:54,409 --> 00:42:56,169
Mr. Moore, you don't have to.

508
00:42:56,759 --> 00:42:59,959
Not tonight, Dad. Tonight you sit.

509
00:43:02,938 --> 00:43:09,058
Hi. Sorry. I'll be quick. My husband
says I talk like I'm billing by the hour.

510
00:43:12,036 --> 00:43:15,626
A few months ago at our engagement
dinner, somebody asked me who

511
00:43:15,676 --> 00:43:19,956
the man pouring the wine was,
and I said he's just our old gardener.

512
00:43:20,764 --> 00:43:23,604
I said it because I was scared
of what you'd think of me.

513
00:43:25,164 --> 00:43:26,804
That's the truth,
so here's the rest of it.

514
00:43:26,854 --> 00:43:30,754
This is my father, Elijah Moore.

515
00:43:31,614 --> 00:43:33,804
He grew every rose in this garden.

516
00:43:33,854 --> 00:43:37,654
He put me through law school with a
part of himself he never got back,

517
00:43:38,514 --> 00:43:42,974
and he never asked me for anything,
not even to say his name.

518
00:43:43,094 --> 00:43:46,794
Dad, everything I am is yours.

519
00:43:53,023 --> 00:43:57,863
Mr. Moore, I'm sorry, I was unforgivable.

520
00:43:58,633 --> 00:44:02,913
Nothin's unforgivable, ma'am.
Sit down, the lamb's gettin' cold.

521
00:44:14,423 --> 00:44:15,843
We match now.

522
00:44:17,961 --> 00:44:18,961
Left.

523
00:44:20,591 --> 00:44:21,671
Left.

524
00:44:23,491 --> 00:44:26,611
Good. Keeps us even.

525
00:44:28,789 --> 00:44:30,649
Hold your head up, baby girl.

526
00:44:32,169 --> 00:44:34,769
It's up, Dad. It's up.
